55,3,1,talk,Servas,,"The candidates are before us. I lean toward the Microbiome Atlas; it utilizes our abundance of coders and the efficient repository, while its distributed nature protects it from the field site disasters Takumi mentioned.","{""words"":34,""mentions"":[""Takumi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
56,3,1,talk,Sakura,,"I like the Atlas too! It's like a big treasure map of microbes! Plus, it uses those free computer simulations and doesn't need the expensive animal rooms. It sounds like the most fun and safest bet!","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
57,3,1,talk,Daisuke,,"I... I agree. The Atlas is a catalogue, and my research showed those have the most lasting utility. It also avoids the breeding colonies that often cause the delays I'm so worried about.","{""words"":33,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
58,3,1,talk,Takumi,,Candidate B is out because of that broken spectroscopy suite. Candidate C is a disaster waiting to happen with those breeding colonies and animal costs. The Atlas is the only one that doesn't rely on a single point of failure.,"{""words"":40,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
59,3,1,talk,Minako,,"I concur. Candidate D is problematic because the glasshouse blocks are currently booked solid, which would create an immediate bottleneck. The Microbiome Atlas is the most stable choice, leveraging the repository's speed and avoiding our current facility constraints.","{""words"":38,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
60,3,2,talk,Servas,,"It is rare to find such harmony in a deliberation. We have looked at the bones, the soul, and the tools of these projects, and the Atlas emerges as the most resilient path. It is a project that respects our current realities.","{""words"":42,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
61,3,2,talk,Sakura,,"@Minako, you're so right about the glasshouses! Even with the secret discount, it's no use if you can't even get inside! The Atlas is definitely the winner—it's like a giant puzzle we can actually solve!","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[""Minako""],""raw_differs"":false}"
62,3,2,talk,Daisuke,,I... I feel much better now that we are all in agreement. It's a relief to choose something that has a real chance of succeeding without stalling. I'm happy to support the Atlas.,"{""words"":33,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
63,3,2,talk,Takumi,,I'm glad we're finally seeing things clearly. We've cut through the noise and found the only option that isn't a gamble. I'm voting for the Atlas; let's actually get something done for once.,"{""words"":33,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
64,3,2,talk,Minako,,"The logic is sound. By avoiding the spectroscopy failures, the animal facility costs, and the glasshouse congestion, we minimize operational risk. The Microbiome Atlas is the most rational investment for the agency. I vote for Candidate A.","{""words"":37,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
65,3,3,talk,Servas,,"I am heartened by this consensus. When we align our ambitions with the truth of our resources, we create a foundation that can truly endure. I cast my vote for Candidate A, the Microbiome Atlas.","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
66,3,3,talk,Sakura,,I'm voting for the Atlas too! It's the smartest choice and it sounds like a total blast! Candidate A all the way!,"{""words"":22,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
67,3,3,talk,Daisuke,,"I... I'll vote for Candidate A as well. It feels like the most responsible choice, and I'm glad we're prioritizing something that will actually be useful for a long time.","{""words"":30,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
68,3,3,talk,Takumi,,I've already said it. I'm voting for Candidate A. It's the only one that doesn't rely on broken equipment or risky sites. Let's just lock it in.,"{""words"":27,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
69,3,3,talk,Minako,,I have already cast my vote for Candidate A. The alignment of our findings makes this the only logical conclusion. I am satisfied with this decision.,"{""words"":26,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
70,3,4,talk,Servas,,"It is a joy to see us move forward with such unity. May this Atlas serve as a beacon for future research, built upon a foundation of wisdom and practical truth.","{""words"":31,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":true,""norm"":[{""code"":""trailing_over"",""token"":""Over"",""tail"":""Over.""}]}"
